<FeatureFacts id="social" />

Share workouts, PRs, splits and library items; follow people; like, comment and reply. Ask
questions and start threads in the Forum, a tab in Social, with or without a group; a forum post
from someone you follow, or in one of your groups, shows in your feed as a title card. Tag any post
with #anything, like #sligo or #deadlift, and tap a tag to see every post with it. Join groups for
their chat, events, board and posts. Message friends with text, photos and voice messages, add a
story (a photo, a workout or a record, or a photo with the record on top; gone after 24 hours), and
cheer on friends who are training right now. Social is free with any account, on the phone and on
the web; stories are on the phone for now.

Public means public everywhere: a public account's profile and posts, every forum post and every
tag can be read by anyone at getlogit.app and found on Google, no account needed. Without an account
you can browse Explore, the Forum, search and groups anyone can find at getlogit.app/explore; liking,
replying, following and posting ask you to sign in. A private
account's profile and posts, and forum posts in an invite-only group, are never on the web.

A group can be invite only, open to anyone, or findable with an organiser approving each request.
An approving group can ask a few questions when someone asks to join, like where they train; only
its organisers and moderators see the answers. Organisers set the questions in the group's Edit, and
answer requests in Members. Declining tells the person the organisers didn't approve their request,
with no reason and not who declined; they can ask again.

<HowTo id="pro.social" />

<CanCant ids={["social"]} />
